# Standalone Video Generation Config Template

Use this template when building a JSON config directly (without using `generate_video_config.py` helper).

## Structure

```json
{
    "params": {
        "prompt": "Your video prompt text",
        "model_type": "ltx2",
        "base_model_type": "ltx2",
        "num_inference_steps": 8,
        "cfg_scale": 3.5,
        "seed": 42,
        "fps": 24,
        "video_length": 480,
        "width": 768,
        "height": 480,
        "image_profile": 4,
        "video_profile": 4,
        "audio_profile": 3.5,
        "loras": [
            {
                "name": "Pixar_Toon",
                "multiplier": 1.5,
                "path": "loras/ltx2/Pixar_Toon.safetensors"
            }
        ],
        "attention": "sage2",
        "dtype": "fp16",
        "compile": true,
        "multi_prompts_gen_type": "FG"
    }
}
```

## Key fields

| Field | Description | Default | Notes |
|-------|-------------|---------|-------|
| `prompt` | Full video prompt (single string, no line breaks) | required | Use director-style prompting |
| `model_type` | Model identifier | `ltx2` | Must match a model in `_settings.json` |
| `num_inference_steps` | Denoising steps | 8 | Higher = better quality but slower |
| `cfg_scale` | Classifier-free guidance | 3.5 | 3-5 typical range |
| `seed` | Random seed for reproducibility | 42 | Same seed + same prompt = same output |
| `fps` | Frames per second | 24 | LTX-2.3 default |
| `video_length` | Total frames | 480 | For 20s at 24fps: 480; 10s: 240 |
| `width` | Video width in pixels | 768 | Aspect ratio affects this |
| `height` | Video height in pixels | 480 | For 16:9: 1280x720, for 9:16: 480x720 |
| `loras` | List of LoRA configs | empty array | Style LoRAs need multiplier ≥ 1.5 |
| `attention` | Attention mechanism | `sage2` | `sage2` or `sdpa` |
| `dtype` | Precision | `fp16` | `fp16` or `bf16` |
| `compile` | TorchInductor compile | false | `true` speeds up subsequent runs |
| `multi_prompts_gen_type` | Prompt processing mode | `FG` | `FG` = all lines are one prompt |
| `image_profile` | Inference profile | 4 | GPU VRAM budget level (1-4, higher = more VRAM) |
| `video_profile` | Video profile | 4 | Same as image_profile |

## Aspect ratio guide

| Aspect | Resolution | Width × Height |
|--------|-----------|----------------|
| 16:9 Landscape | HD | 1280 × 720 |
| 16:9 Landscape | 4K | 2048 × 1152 |
| 9:16 Portrait | Reels/Shorts | 480 × 720 |
| 1:1 Square | — | 512 × 512 |

## LoRA format

```json
"loras": [
    {
        "name": "Pixar_Toon",
        "multiplier": 1.5,
        "path": "loras/ltx2/Pixar_Toon.safetensors"
    }
]
```

Style LoRAs (Pixar_Toon, Fantasy_Realism, etc.) need multiplier **≥ 1.0**, typically 1.5 for visible effect. Default 0.5 produces no visible change.

## Usage

1. Save this JSON to a `.json` file
2. Run: `wgp.py --process <config.json> --output-dir <output-dir> --compile --attention sage2 --profile 4 --fp16`
3. Output videos go into the specified output directory